From 7a3365d814b1e3fe1bd06f61c35f40891e814d50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Release Radar <release-radar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:05:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Faster streaming over a tunnel; listening sessions in the
 player

- ExoPlayer keeps 60s of audio behind the playhead (back buffer) so the
  auto-rewind after a pause plays from memory instead of a new request;
  60s/300s forward buffer, 5s rebuffer threshold (was 20s)
- one shared OkHttp client with an IPv4-first resolver for API calls, the
  ping client and the player's streaming data source (OkHttp 4.9 tries
  addresses sequentially, so a VPN with non-routing IPv6 stalled every connect)
- a VPN counts as a network in the connectivity check (upstream #1702)
- socket.io reconnects sooner (5s max delay, 10s attempt timeout)
- Listening sessions for the current book from the player menu: the server's
  sessions for this item, grouped by day, tap to continue from where one ended

